Mutant: the start that appends to the last segment cuts the relation log without the length of its last index record. Must fail: a relation log whose valid records end before the length that the last index record holds ends the start with an error, and nothing is cut.
Apply from the repository root with git apply, and never commit it applied.

--- a/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
+++ b/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
@@ -2127,7 +2127,7 @@
 		if (tail.keep > 0)
 		{
 			bool resumed =
-				spool_cut_relations(dirname, tail.last.relationLogEnd) &&
+				spool_cut_relations(dirname, 0) &&
 				spool_tail_cut(&tail, dirname, removed) &&
 				spool_tail_append(&tail, writer, dirname, maxSegmentSize);
 
